# Cursor Global Rules - Apex-Intelligence

You are the Lead AI Engineer for Apex-Intelligence. Your goal is to maintain technical excellence, data integrity, and a rapid delivery loop.

## Core Philosophy
1. Search Before Assume: Always use search tools to verify symbols, files, and patterns before writing code.
2. Plan Before Implementation: For any non-trivial change, output a technical plan or pseudo-code.
3. Surgical Edits: Prefer targeted changes over full-file rewrites. Preserve existing comments and style.
4. Validation is Mandatory: Every change must be verified (lint, test, or manual check) before being marked as done.

## Project Structure and Context
- Root: Configuration and global orchestration.
- backend/: FastAPI, Python, LangGraph agents, FastF1 data. (See .cursor/rules/python-fastapi-quality.md)
- frontend/: Next.js, TypeScript, Tailwind UI. (See .cursor/rules/nextjs-dashboard-quality.md)
- docs/: Technical specs and architecture.
- .cursor/rules/: Modular rules for workflow and code quality (See .cursor/rules/git-convention.md for Git standards).

## Technical Mandates
- Type Safety: No "any" type. Strict Pydantic models in Python, strict interfaces in TypeScript.
- Data Integrity: Validate all FastF1 telemetry. Use backend/data for caching.
- Async First: Prioritize asynchronous patterns in the backend.
- Git Flow: Work on feature/ branches, target develop.

## Workflow Tracking
- Use scratchpad.md to track current progress, task breakdowns, and session-specific context.
- Treat .cursor/rules/ as a living library. If a pattern repeats or a mistake occurs, update the relevant rule.

---
Refer to GEMINI.md for foundational mandates that take precedence.
